Usage: ptx [OPTION]... [FILE]...

Produce a permuted index of file contents.

OPTIONS:
  -A, --auto-reference       output automatically generated references
  -C, --copyright            display copyright and version
  -G, --traditional          use traditional non-GNU word splitting
  -F, --flag-truncation ARG  string used for line truncation
  -M, --macro-name ARG       macro name for formatted output
  -O                         generate output as roff directives [DIFFERS:
                             --format=roff not supported]
  -R, --right-side-refs      put references in right margin
  -S, --sentence-regexp ARG  regexp for sentence ends
  -T                         generate output as TeX directives [DIFFERS:
                             --format=tex not supported]
  -W, --word-regexp ARG      regexp for words
  -b, --break-file ARG       file containing word break characters
  -f, --ignore-case          fold lower case to upper case for sorting
  -g, --gap-size NUM         gap size in columns between output fields
  -i, --ignore-file ARG      ignore words from file
  -o, --only-file ARG        only output words from file
  -r, --references           first input field is reference
  -t, --typeset-mode         output for troff or nroff
  -w, --width NUM            output width in columns, reference excluded
      --help                 display this help and exit
  -V, --version              output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
